Subject: [PATCH] webgl: withhold extensions the claimed device does not expose

Measured against a real Windows machine with an Intel UHD 630, our build
advertises three WebGL extensions it never sees:

  WEBGL_compressed_texture_astc
  WEBGL_compressed_texture_etc
  WEBGL_compressed_texture_etc1

These are mobile and Apple compressed-texture formats. SwiftShader supports them
and a Windows D3D11 machine does not, so a profile claiming Windows advertised a
set no Windows Chrome reports. Fingerprinting scripts hash the extension list,
so three extra entries are enough to match nothing real.

Only removal is implemented, and that asymmetry is the design rather than a
limitation. Adding an extension cannot be done safely: a page calls
getExtension() and then calls methods on the object it receives, so one claimed
but unimplemented fails at first use — the same shape as claiming a WebGL limit
the driver cannot meet, which patch 0026 exists to prevent. Removal has no such
failure mode; the page is told no exactly as the real device would tell it.

Served at ExtensionSupportedAndAllowed, which both getSupportedExtensions() and
getExtension() run through, so the list and the objects obtainable from it
cannot disagree. Withholding from the list alone would leave getExtension()
handing out an extension the list denies, which is a worse contradiction than
the one being fixed.

The profile carries WebGL extension names as getSupportedExtensions() spells
them, not GL names — the two are different namespaces, and ANGLE's existing
disabled-extension machinery works on the GL side, so it is the wrong layer for
a list captured from a browser.

An empty list in the profile disables the filter entirely, so a profile that
does not describe its extensions does not silently lose all of them.

Note this closes the removable half of the gap. Our host still lacks two
extensions the reference has on WebGL1 and five on WebGL2 —
KHR_parallel_shader_compile, WEBGL_blend_func_extended and friends — and those
cannot be added for the reason above. They are a host capability question, the
same class as the render limits raised in patch 0027.

Ledger: webgl.extensions.
diff --git a/base/apostate/profile.cc b/base/apostate/profile.cc
index 709e5bd..696db16 100644
--- a/base/apostate/profile.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.cc
@@ -229,6 +229,14 @@ Profile* Profile::ParseOrNull(const std::string& encoded) {
     }
   }
 
+  if (const ListValue* exts = dict->FindList("gl_extensions")) {
+    for (const auto& v : *exts) {
+      if (const std::string* s = v.GetIfString()) {
+        profile->gl_extensions_.insert(*s);
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   if (const DictValue* keyboard = dict->FindDict("keyboard")) {
     if (const DictValue* map = keyboard->FindDict("layout_map")) {
       for (const auto [code, value] : *map) {
diff --git a/base/apostate/profile.h b/base/apostate/profile.h
index 77bd5b3..a077b58 100644
--- a/base/apostate/profile.h
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.h
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <map>
+#include <set>
 #include <optional>
 #include <string>
 
@@ -202,6 +203,17 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
   // validates every allocation against the value it reported.
   const std::map<std::string, int>& gl_limits() const { return gl_limits_; }
 
+  // WebGL extension names the claimed device exposes, as
+  // getSupportedExtensions() spells them.
+  //
+  // Used only to *remove* extensions this host advertises and the claimed
+  // device does not. Adding one is not possible and must not be attempted: a
+  // page calls getExtension() and then calls methods on the object it gets
+  // back, so an extension claimed but unimplemented fails at first use. Removal
+  // has no such failure mode — the page is simply told no, exactly as it would
+  // be on the real device.
+  const std::set<std::string>& gl_extensions() const { return gl_extensions_; }
+
   // IANA timezone name, e.g. "Europe/Warsaw".
   //
   // Only the zone *name* is a host fact. ICU's data is compiled into the binary
@@ -286,6 +298,7 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
   std::optional<int> media_videoinput_count_;
   std::map<std::string, std::string> keyboard_layout_map_;
   std::map<std::string, int> gl_limits_;
+  std::set<std::string> gl_extensions_;
   std::optional<std::string> timezone_;
   std::optional<bool> prefers_dark_;
   std::optional<std::string> accept_languages_;
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
index fb1bc7c..045a3e5 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
@@ -25,6 +25,10 @@
 
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.h"
 
+#include <set>
+
+#include "base/apostate/profile.h"
+
 #include <inttypes.h>
 
 #include <memory>
@@ -3839,6 +3843,27 @@ bool WebGLRenderingContextBase::ExtensionSupportedAndAllowed(
     return false;
   if (disabled_extensions_.Contains(String(tracker->ExtensionName())))
     return false;
+
+  // Withhold extensions the claimed device does not expose.
+  //
+  // Measured: SwiftShader advertises WEBGL_compressed_texture_astc, _etc and
+  // _etc1 — mobile and Apple compressed-texture formats — which a Windows
+  // D3D11 machine never exposes. The extension list is hashed by fingerprinting
+  // scripts, so three extra entries make the hash match no real Windows Chrome.
+  //
+  // This is the removal direction only, and that is the whole point. Adding an
+  // extension is unsafe because a page calls getExtension() and then calls
+  // methods on the object; removal cannot fail, because the page is told no
+  // exactly as the real device would tell it. Serving here rather than at
+  // getSupportedExtensions() covers both, since getExtension() reaches the same
+  // check — a list and an object that disagreed would be worse than either.
+  if (const base::apostate::Profile* profile = base::apostate::Profile::Get()) {
+    const std::set<std::string>& allowed = profile->gl_extensions();
+    if (!allowed.empty() &&
+        allowed.find(std::string(tracker->ExtensionName())) == allowed.end()) {
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
   return true;
 }
 
